  "id": "Compound::DB04845 - Gene::84617",
  "verbalization": "Ixabepilone is implicated in the inhibition of microtubules, a mechanism shared with Cabazitaxel and Eribulin, all of which bind to Tubb6. The evidence suggests that Ixabepilone, through its interaction with Eribulin, ultimately contributes to the binding of Tubb6. This is supported by the shared lowest common ancestors in the pathways, which point to Tubulin Binding Agents and Cyclic Ethers as central molecular entities. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Ixabepilone, via Eribulin, exerts its effect on Tubb6, likely through a common molecular interaction. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between Ixabepilone and Tubb6, mediated by Eribulin, and underscores the role of microtubule inhibition in this process.",
